    "name": "Does Bathroom Vanity Replacement Require a Permit in San Diego?",
    "text": "Does Bathroom Vanity Replacement Require a Permit in San Diego?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Whether a bathroom vanity replacement needs a permit depends on the exact work and the authority having jurisdiction. A like-for-like cabinet and fixture change may be treated differently from relocating plumbing, altering drain or supply piping, changing electrical work, removing wallboard, or modifying the layout, so confirm the scope with the contractor and local building department before work starts.",
